  "worked_solution": "- $M$ is an identity matrix. First, it's a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. Also, its entries on the main diagonal are all ones, and the rest of the entries are zeros.\n\n- $N$ is *not* an identity matrix since it's not a square matrix.\n\n- $P$ is *not* an identity matrix. Although it's a diagonal matrix, its diagonal entries are not all ones.\n\nTherefore, only $M$ is an identity matrix.",
